import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'dungeon':('Dungeon: recognized Enlightenment potion','The Warrior has a known Enlightenment potion and cannot see stairs beyond a wall. The original leaves the potion unused and those stairs unknown. The correction drinks one and the native game reveals the stairs.'),
 'town-control':('Control: Enlightenment in town','The existing rule forbids drinking Enlightenment in town. Both versions keep it.'),
 'unknown-control':('Control: potion flavor still unknown','Neither version assumes an unidentified potion is Enlightenment. Both keep it.'),
 'unrelated-control':('Control: unrelated True Seeing potion','This useful-item routine does not automatically drink unrelated True Seeing potions. Both versions keep it.'),
 'augmentation-dungeon':('Control: Augmentation in the dungeon','Augmentation already works here. Both versions drink it and leave the remote stairs unknown.'),
 'augmentation-town':('Control: Augmentation in town','The town restriction belongs to Enlightenment, not Augmentation. Both versions still drink Augmentation in town.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text();frames=[json.loads(l[6:]) for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith('FRAME ')]
  assert len(frames)==2
  match=re.search(r'OUTCOME (.*)',raw);outcome={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])}
  assert frames[0]['potions']-frames[1]['potions']==outcome['potions_spent']
  item[phase]={'frames':frames,'outcome':outcome,'raw':raw}
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The unused Enlightenment potion</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f3f1eb;color:#273a3b;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.discovery{font-size:30px;font-weight:750}.count{font-size:23px}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native item choice, potion use and map knowledge</p><h1>The Borg recognizes Enlightenment but never drinks it</h1><p>A Warrior carries a known Enlightenment potion in the dungeon, with stairs beyond a wall still unknown. The original useful-item routine leaves the potion unused and those stairs unknown. After the correction it drinks one potion, and the native game reveals the stairs.</p><p>Enlightenment reveals the level's layout. This is a utility fix: no faster escape, avoided attack, injury or death is measured. The existing rule against drinking it in town remains.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><button data-step="0">Start</button><button data-step="1">Show item use</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="discovery"></div><p class="count"></p><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="corrected" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="discovery"></div><p class="count"></p><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>Why the correction works</h2><p>The potion is recognized and its town restriction checked, but the original branch never requests a drink. The correction adds the missing drink inside that branch. Five complete control logs stay identical: town, unknown flavor, unrelated potion, and Augmentation in town and dungeon.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior level 40, depth 30 (town controls use depth 0), seed 1000, light, food and a quiet constructed arena. A wall blocks the stair ten squares to the east, with a passage around its end. Native line of sight and player knowledge confirm that the stair is unknown. The actual Borg safety check accepts the location.</p><p>The test calls the real useful-item routine, validates the exact queued potion, then native potion use computes its effect and reveals the stair in the player's map memory. No map knowledge, replacement potion or successful effect is injected.</p><p>This isolates the utility action, not the whole exploration/caution loop. The town controls use the same constructed arena at depth 0, not a generated town/store visit. No monster turns, route choice, travel time or survival improvement are tested. The potion cost is real: the correction consumes one item to obtain that information.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="corrected-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/81">issue81 / CBUG-0065</a>. Discovery credit: borg-rs.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['corrected','after']]){let d=c[phase],f=d.frames[step],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.discovery').textContent=f.stairs_known?'Down stairs discovered':'Stairs still unknown';p.querySelector('.count').textContent=`${f.potions} potions remaining`;p.querySelector('.stats').textContent=`Warrior HP: ${f.hp}.`;p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===0?'Before checking useful items.':d.outcome.used?'Drinks one selected potion.':'No potion requested; inventory unchanged.';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='dungeon'?'Recorded discovery: original leaves the stairs unknown; correction drinks Enlightenment and reveals them.':'Unchanged control: same potion use and map knowledge in both versions.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
